    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), both of whom are primary targets for production against favorable pitching matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-upside environment against Warren, with a 16% park boost and a massive platoon edge driving his elite status. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** leverages a high-efficiency matchup against Stock, where a positive wind shift and a distinct SP skill advantage elevate him into the top tier of our daily output. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.09) round out our high-leverage core, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically benefiting from a soft matchup against Bassitt that projects well beyond his base metrics.\n\nOur roster strategy for today prioritizes high-order volume and favorable park factors, though we must navigate a few marginal start risks. **Sam Antonacci** (61.82) earns a spot in the lineup largely due to his leadoff positioning, which helps mitigate the threat posed by Holmes. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Wade Meckler** (46.94), who narrowly missed the starting nine; while his leadoff order spot was enticing, he fell just short of the efficiency floor established by our OF/UTIL depth, making him the odd man out in a crowded field. We continue to monitor the absence of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as their continued status on the IL limits our ceiling in power-heavy categories. \n\nRisks are relatively contained today, but owners should be wary of the \"Elite Hold\" SP profiles facing **Miguel Vargas** and **Heliot Ramos**. Both hitters face arms that suppress stolen base attempts (53% and 63% hold rates, respectively), which complicates our scarcity-focused strategy for SB accumulation. While **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** sit in the 54-57 range, their production remains essential to maintaining our floor; we have benched **Wade Meckler** and are tracking **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** closely for any shifts in late-inning availability or injury status. No major weather concerns are currently flagged, meaning we expect these projections to hold steady throughout the slate.",
